\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. FRIEND of the home, as when in Galilee
\par The mothers brought their little ones to Thee,
\par So we, dear Lord, would now the children bring,
\par And seek for them the shelter of Thy wing.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thine are they, by Thy love's eternal claim,
\par Thine we baptize them in the threefold Name:
\par Yet not the sign we trust, Lord, but the grace
\par That in Thy fold prepared the lambs a place.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Lord, may Thy church, as with a mother's care,
\par For Thee the lambs within her bosom bear;
\par And grant, as morning fades to noon, that they
\par Still in her love and holy service stay.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Draw through the child the parents nearer Thee.
\par Endue their home with growing sanctity:
\par And gather all, by earthly homes made one.
\par In heaven, O Christ, when earthly days are done.
\par                                            Amen.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

